      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "T-S J1.4 , r, right [Col. II]",
          "value": "<p></p>\n\n<ol><li>Also dis[p]ensed for them</li>\n<li>on Tuesday the 18th</li>\n<li>of that (month) five qin\u1e6d\u0101rs (500 pounds)</li>\n<li>b. Dani\u02beel 8 the slave girl of Mukht\u0101r 2</li>\n<li>the man from Ba\u02bfalbek 5 Umm Khalaf 3</li>\n<li>the female washer of the dead for Fustat 2 b. Shekhanya 6</li>\n<li>the cantor al-Qu\u1e0d\u0101\u02bf\u012b (healer of stomach ailments) 6 Sib\u0101\u02bf 3</li>\n<li>the wife of the man from Sicily 3 Ab\u016b Shaykha 2</li>\n<li>the Maghrebi woman 2 Ma\u02bfl\u0101\u02be 3</li>\n<li>the son of the deaf man 8 the man from Mal\u012bj 5</li>\n<li>the son of Ab\u016b Sa\u02bf\u012bd and his divorc&eacute;e 5 Sulaym\u0101n 2</li>\n<li>Sham\u012b\u02bfa 4 b. Natan 2</li>\n<li>\u1e24asan the glassmaker 3 Barak\u0101t and his father-in-law 5</li>\n<li>al-S\u016br\u0101n\u012b 4 Ab\u016b Mukht\u0101r 7</li>\n<li>Furayj <del>3</del> 2 Umm Hill\u0101la 1</li>\n<li>Zuhayr 3 the female washer of the dead and her daughter 2</li>\n<li>the acquaintance of the dyer 4 the son of the <i>\u1e25aver</i> Mena\u1e25em 3</li>\n<li>Umm Furayj 1 Avraham of Tyre 3</li>\n<li>the woman from Mal\u012bj 1 Sal\u0101ma 3</li>\n<li>Umm Ibrahim 2 b. [al-\u02bfA]mm\u0101n\u012b <del>3</del> 5</li>\n<li>Umm \u1e92arifa 3 <del>2</del> the [man from A]cre 6</li>\n<li>Ya\u02bfaqov the blind man 2 the m[other-in-la]w of Mu\u1e6d\u0101lib\u012b 2</li>\n<li>b. al-Murahhi\u1e6d (son of the writer/singer of liturgical poetry) 2 b. al-K\u0101mukh\u012b (son of the preparer of vinegar sauce) 2</li>\n<li>Yosef and his brothers 8 b. al-Kharaz\u012b (the son of the maker of beads) 1</li>\n<li>Umm S\u0101lim 2 the mother-in-law of the woman from Palestine 3</li>\n<li>the silk worker 4 <del>Aharon from Jerusalem</del></li>\n<li>\u1e62\u0101li\u1e25 4 the man from the \u1e24ij\u0101z 3</li>\n<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<del>159</del> 163</li></ol>\n",
